  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We have,\r\n$$\r\na x^{2}+b x+1=0\r\n$$\r\nFor real roots, $D \\geq 0$\r\n$$\r\n\\therefore \\quad b^{2}-4 a \\geq 0\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad b^{2} \\geq 4 a$\r\n$\\therefore(a, b)=(1,2),(1,3),(2,3)$\r\n$\\therefore$ Number of ordered pairs $(a, b)=3$ and $a$ is always less than $b$.",
